    "aspect": "16:9",
    "description": "A learning video from MEDAS 2.0 (beta). Moving live data from a personal-account database to a team-owned one, a hand-written migration script copied every document but recreated every index under MongoDB's default name. Weeks later a fresh instance of the live service failed to boot: the app asked for its named index on the same keys and MongoDB refused (IndexOptionsConflict, code 85). The old database was already deactivated, so the fix went into code: an idempotent index helper used for every collection. Lessons: mongodump/mongorestore, compare indexes before retiring the source, keep the source until verified, log skipped conflicts, versioned migrations.",
    "note": "No people are named. Code and log views are labeled illustrations of the pattern, not the original script or a captured log. MEDAS is in beta with a small number of clinical users; the dev database holds example test data only.",
