    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "FRAMEWORK",
      "role_note": "FRAMEWORK beat -- the one idea the story turns on: an index has keys AND a name",
      "narration_text": "First, the one idea this story turns on. A MongoDB index has two separate properties: what it indexes, meaning the field and its sort order, and its name, which is just a label. If you don't pass a name, MongoDB makes one up from the field, like username underscore l c underscore one. Same index, different label.",
