      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "THE RULE",
      "role_note": "the MongoDB rule that turns a label into a crash",
      "narration_text": "And here's the rule that matters. If an index already exists on a field, and you ask for another index on the same field under a different name, MongoDB refuses. It won't guess whether you meant a duplicate. It raises an error: Index Options Conflict, code eighty-five.",
