      "act": "WHY NOBODY NOTICED",
      "role_note": "why the bug stayed dormant",
      "narration_text": "Why did nobody notice? Queries only care what an index covers, not what it's called, so everything kept working. The names only matter when the app starts, because that's when it creates its indexes. As long as no fresh instance booted, the problem stayed hidden.",
