      "act": "THE CRASH",
      "role_note": "labeled illustration of the startup failure (not a captured log)",
      "narration_text": "Weeks later, the live service started a fresh instance. On boot, the app asked for its named index on the username field. MongoDB found that field already indexed as username underscore l c underscore one, and refused. Because index setup runs at startup, the worker failed to boot. With only a few users in beta, the impact was small, but the cause was weeks old.",
