    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "act": "THE CAVEAT",
      "role_note": "FALSIFIABILITY beat -- where the fix itself is weak",
      "narration_text": "One honest caveat. Skipping errors has a cost. If someone later changes an index on purpose, a silent skip would hide that too. So every skip should log a warning, and a mature system handles index changes as versioned, reviewed migrations, not as startup code.",
